---
description: Never push branches or tags to origin; leave publishing to the user
alwaysApply: true
---

# Never push to origin

Do not push to any remote.

Never run:

- `git push` (any form, including `-u`, `--tags`, or a named remote)
- `gh stack submit` or other commands that push branches as a side effect

Local commits, branches, and PR body drafts are fine when the user asks for them. After a local commit or branch is ready, tell the user the push command (for example `git push -u origin HEAD`) and let them run it.

If a workflow (PR create, stack submit) requires a push first, stop and ask the user to push, then continue with `gh` only after the remote branch exists.
